            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic significance of the symptoms associated with prostatic carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>270-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper discusses the prognostic significance of the symptoms of prostatic carcinoma. In a series of 123 patients, 72 presented with prostatism, of which 11% died with progressive malignant disease. Of 36 patients with retention of urine, 30% died with progressive malignant disease, and of 15 patients with a combination of skeletal pain and prostatism, 53% died of progressive malignant disease. Skeletal pain is a very poor prognostic factor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
